Package: rts2-python
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: rts2-db
Description: Remote Telescope System 2 - Python client scripting support
 RTS2 (Remote Telescope System, 2nd version) is a distributed control
 system for robotic astronomical observatories.
 .
 This package contains rts2.scriptcomm, the Python library RTS2's "exe"
 observation scripts use to talk to the running system (device values,
 state, exposures, image handling, ...), plus a set of ready-to-use
 system scripts - guiding, sky flats, filter-synchronized multi-camera
 sequences, GRB follow-up, an idle-time sky survey, an airmass scan -
 installed to /usr/share/rts2/scripts, with /etc/rts2/scripts kept as a
 symlink to it. rts2-base's script-path resolution (see [scriptexec]
 script_path in rts2.ini, defaulting to /etc/rts2/scripts) finds
 anything there by bare filename, e.g. "exe guideccd.py", without every
 target/camera needing a full path. Pure Python, no compiled
 extensions; the same setup.py this package builds from is also
 directly pip-installable.
